From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:30:53 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: bound the console read when the device
 reads all ones

brcmf_pcie_bus_console_read() reads the firmware's console write index
and walks read_idx up to it, wrapping at bufsize. When the device is
gone the index reads 0xffffffff, which read_idx never reaches, and the
walk never ends.

Seen on a BCM4383 after s2idle on the Pixel 9a: the chip does not come
back, the reset work entered this loop from brcmf_pcie_reset() and spun
one CPU at 100 % with a stream of "CONSOLE:" lines of 0xff bytes. A
later rmmod then blocked in cancel_work_sync() for good, holding the
device lock, so the next shutdown would have hung in device_shutdown().

Return when the write index is outside the console buffer.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 785a8f13c..4ca80e15e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -1226,6 +1226,14 @@ static void brcmf_pcie_bus_console_read(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 		return;
 	addr = console->base_addr + BRCMF_CONSOLE_WRITEIDX_OFFSET;
 	newidx = brcmf_pcie_read_tcm32(devinfo, addr);
+	if (newidx >= console->bufsize) {
+		/* A dead link reads all ones, and read_idx wraps at bufsize,
+		 * so the loop below would never meet it.
+		 */
+		brcmf_err(bus, "console write index %u out of range (%u)\n",
+			  newidx, console->bufsize);
+		return;
+	}
 	while (newidx != console->read_idx) {
 		addr = console->buf_addr + console->read_idx;
 		ch = brcmf_pcie_read_tcm8(devinfo, addr);
